hether it  be their lore or what makes them so fun  and especially if this isn't the first  time you're hearing my voice i'm talking  to you then 90 out there you should  consider subscribing to the channel  you'll get notified of my new uploads  which chances are will be about games  you love and you can always unsubscribe  if you change your mind either way i  look forward to seeing you around number  one nicholas egg this is probably the  most obvious pick of the bunch and for  good reason for those who are unfamiliar  with the character of mikola he is the  twin brother of millennia and is a  demigod just like his sister and all of  his step siblings in fact he's the only  demigod in the entire game that we don't  get to kill i mean encounter and like  his sister he's a rare empyrean and has  suffered from afflictions since birth  millennia was cursed to harbor the  scarlet rot inside her body and mykola  is cursed to have the body of a child  forever this may be because their  emperians and outer gods housed their  essence in them or it might be because  they're inbred it depends on who you ask  but despite his appearance mikala was  apparently extremely intelligent  strangely very likable and was somewhat  of an inventor before all went to hell  with the shattering of the elden ring  millennia even describes him as the most  fearsome demigod of them all in regard  to his wisdom and allure prior to being  in this giant egg in moguin palace  underneath the lands between mykola was  actually located way across the land to  the far north where he was nursing his  own great tree called the halig tree  with his own blood you can actually see  the exact spot where he was previously  located which notably features his image  in the roots at the base of the halak  tree where you fight his sister  millennia he was kidnapped from his  position here by his omen laden half  brother named moog while millennia was  off fighting their other half-brother  general radon for other reasons moog  kidnapped mykola because he wanted  mikala an imperian to be the vassal for  the outer god that he was serving called  the formless mother now this is where it  gets even creepier than kidnapping your  half-brother who looks like a child moog  wanted to be the consort of his  half-brother but mikala kept refusing to  do  certain things with moog in his bed  chamber which i suppose is why moog  decided to put mikala in this egg cocoon  thing to germinate or something now  obviously there are a lot of lore  implications in pretty much everything i  just said in fact there's enough there  to make an entire other video or videos  about so i won't go into explaining all  of that right now but that is precisely  why i and many others feel like it would  be a very welcome choice should eldon  ring's dlc feature mykolo awakening from  the egg he's currently in or maybe  having the player enter the egg to be  transported to the dimension of the  formless mother or something like that  it would offer so much on the characters  of both mykola and moog and potentially  some other glimpses into other outer  gods also there's no real reason to  assume he's dead in there since moog  still declares that his mogwin dynasty  is coming to be implying the vassal  mikula isn't dead unless he is and moog  really just like sloshing around in the  blood of his dead siblings which i guess  i wouldn't put past him all things  considered next up would be the lands  outside the lands between any elder ring  player worth their salt knows that there  are multiple different worlds or lands  or areas that exist outside the lands  between that are referenced in the game  you've got the land of the reeds which  is where the race of humans  appropriately named the reeds originates  from it would be a great addition to not  only the world building of elden ring in  general but also to some specific and  very important characters such as queen  america herself who famously comes from  the land of the newman outside the lands  between she's even said to have strong  ties to the black knife assassins who  get this also hail from the land of the  newman and both parties are shrouded in  what should be illegal amounts of  mystery because let's be honest we still  don't know what the hell is going on  with them or how they're connected  exactly especially given that the  assassins killed merica's favorite son  being able to experience an alternate  campaign in one of these far away lands  or even the land where the tarnished  were banished too following their exile  from the lands between would undoubtedly  go a long way to understanding some of  the most integral pieces of eldon ring  lore or it could make things worse i  suppose that's also possible number next  speaking of other lands what about the  lands underneath compared to the  overworld of the lands between we've  only discovered a tiny amount of what  could possibly be explorable areas under  the ground i mean look at all this  unused space but not only would this  physically be a very possible addition  that i could see happening in dlc using  space that's already set in the game but  it would also once again give more  background on important lore which is  very valuable to people like me there  are so many questions that need  answering about the mimic tiers and the  backstories of what happened to the  people groups that used to live in the  eternal cities not to mention the  connections with the race of the  dragonkin which were apparently also  beings that were created to possibly  achieve immortality and of course  there's also godwin who was famously  killed on the night of the black knives  which i alluded to earlier and then all  of a sudden has appeared here underneath  the world at the roots of the great tree  as a giant clam-faced fish man some  answers would be nice and more items and  exploration deon and would most likely  do the trick number four that weird rock  in the oce